{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_019etbcGTsW2oJBAq8dhVW5D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed:\n\n**Task:** `answers/07-001-your-app-gets-1m-queriesday-how-optimize-cost.md`\n\nThe answer note covers the 6-step cost optimization hierarchy for 1M queries/day:\n\n1. **Profile first** — token breakdown (input/output) and cost per query distribution\n2. **Skip the call** — exact-match Redis cache (5-15% hit) + semantic cache via GPTCache at cosine > 0.93 (20-35% hit)\n3. **Route to cheaper model** — complexity classifier sends 60% of FAQ traffic to GPT-4o-mini (16× cheaper than GPT-4o)\n4. **Reduce tokens** — LLMLingua prompt compression (30-50%), cross-encoder reranking to top-3 chunks, max_tokens + conciseness instruction (output tokens cost 3-10× more than input)\n5. **Improve GPU utilization** (self-hosted) — vLLM PagedAttention, batching\n6. **Quantize** (self-hosted) — AWQ/GPTQ INT4 for 4× VRAM reduction\n\nConcrete before/after table shows $10,500/day → ~$900/day (91% reduction). Key pitfalls: ignoring output token cost, missing the self-hosting breakeven threshold (~$50K/month API spend), and adding caching without specifying layer thresholds."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":318,"cache_read_input_tokens":75676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":318,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c3a2b53-88ed-4d23-bcb8-ecbb27a73097","uuid":"a8d4c725-c206-4bd6-8b5c-d3091547c448"}
